# Tab Tool

Manage tabs for the current conversation.

## Primary Rules

1. Keep the workflow in one active tab unless a new tab is clearly necessary.
2. After navigation, look at the returned screenshot before the next action.
3. Prefer `tab view` when you only need a clean screenshot.

## Commands

### tab init
Start a session on a URL.

```json
{ "action": "init", "url": "https://example.com" }
```

### tab open
Open a new tab only when needed.

```json
{ "action": "open", "url": "https://example.com" }
```

### tab switch
Switch to a known `tab_id`.

```json
{ "action": "switch", "tab_id": 123 }
```

### tab list
List tabs when you need to know available `tab_id`s.

```json
{ "action": "list" }
```

### tab view
Get a clean screenshot of the active tab.

```json
{ "action": "view" }
```

### tab refresh
Reload the active tab.

```json
{ "action": "refresh", "tab_id": 123 }
```

### tab back / tab forward
Use browser history when you need to return instead of reopening pages.

```json
{ "action": "back" }
{ "action": "forward" }
```

### tab close
Close an unused tab.

```json
{ "action": "close", "tab_id": 123 }
```

## Recommended Flow

- Start with `tab init`
- If you need to inspect the page, use `tab view`
- Then use the highlight tool to find the next target
